// =============================================================================
// BND-2185 - Backfill of dates on the Data Vault fiscal-code satellite
// =============================================================================
//
// Context (agreed solution - "SOLUZIONE 1", parametric time window)
//   The incremental pipeline `idpay_data_vault_copy` extracts from Cosmos only
//   the records whose technical field `createdAt` falls in a UTC half-open
//   window [fromDate, toDate) and appends the new fiscal codes to `data_vault`
//   (join kind=leftanti on `_id`). Pre-existing rows are never rewritten.
//
// Two one-off preconditions before switching the pipeline to window mode:
//   1. INITIAL FULL LOAD of the current Cosmos `data_vault` content into ADX
//      (the ADX table is currently empty). This can be done by running the
//      pipeline once with a wide window, e.g.
//        fromDate = "1970-01-01T00:00:00Z", toDate = <today 00:00 UTC>
//      only AFTER `createdAt` has been populated upstream (mcshared-datavault);
//      otherwise perform a dedicated full copy.
//   2. This BACKFILL, to stamp `loadDate`, `updateDate` and `createdAt` on the
//      rows loaded by the initial full load that still have NULL dates (e.g.
//      historical documents created before `createdAt` existed upstream).
//
// Why it is required
//   After `.create-merge` adds the nullable `loadDate`/`updateDate`/`createdAt`
//   columns, the rows loaded by the initial full load keep NULL dates. The
//   window-based pipeline never rewrites them, so without this backfill they
//   would stay NULL forever. This stamps them once with a stable, explicit
//   migration timestamp.
//
// Execution
//   Run MANUALLY, exactly once, against the `idpay` database, AFTER the schema
//   change (create_tables_idpay.kql) is applied and the initial full load is
//   done, and BEFORE enabling the daily window-based run. Idempotent: rows that
//   already have the dates are left untouched (coalesce).
//
// Notes
//   - Adjust `backfill_ts` to the agreed historical/migration timestamp.
//   - `createdAt` is set to `backfill_ts` only when unknown (historical rows);
//     rows loaded with a real source `createdAt` keep it.
//   - The fiscal code lives in column `data` (PII): it is never projected to
//     logs here, only `_id`, `page` and the technical columns are rewritten.
// =============================================================================

.set-or-replace data_vault <|
let backfill_ts = datetime(2026-10-23T00:00:00Z);
data_vault
| extend loadDate = coalesce(loadDate, backfill_ts)
| extend updateDate = coalesce(updateDate, loadDate, backfill_ts)
| extend createdAt = coalesce(createdAt, backfill_ts)
| project _id, data, page, loadDate, updateDate, createdAt

